As an AI assistant, I would like to correct that the code you provided is for a Linux shell command line, not Swift. If you are looking to translate a sentence in Swift, you can use the Google Translate API or other translation APIs available. Here is an example of how to use the Google Translate API in Swift:
1. First, you need to obtain an API key from the Google Cloud Console.
2. Add the following code to your Swift file:
```swift
import Foundation
func translate(_ text: String, to language: String, completion: @escaping (String?, Error?) -> Void) {
    let apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY_HERE"
    let url = URL(string: "https://translation.googleapis.com/language/translate/v2?key=\(apiKey)")!
    var request = URLRequest(url: url)
    request.httpMethod = "POST"
    request.addValue("application/json", forHTTPHeaderField: "Content-Type")
    request.addValue(Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier ?? "", forHTTPHeaderField: "X-Ios-Bundle-Identifier")
    let data = """
    {
        "q": "\(text)",
        "target": "\(language)"
    }
    """.data(using: .utf8)!
    request.httpBody = data
    let task = URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: request) { (data, response, error) in
        guard let data = data else {
            completion(nil, error)
            return
        }
        do {
            let json = try JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: data, options: []) as! [String: Any]
            let translations = json["data"] as! [String: Any]
            let translatedText = translations["translations"] as! [[String: Any]]
            let translation = translatedText.first!["translatedText"] as! String
            completion(translation, nil)
        } catch {
            completion(nil, error)
        }
    }
    task.resume()
}
```
3. To use the function, call it with the text you want to translate and the target language code:
```swift
translate("I have been to Europe twice", to: "es") { (translation, error) in
    if let error = error {
        print("Error: \(error.localizedDescription)")
    } else if let translation = translation {
        print("Translated text: \(translation)")
    }
}
```
This will output the translated text in the console. Note that the target language code "es" is for Spanish. You can change it to any other language code supported by the Google Translate API.

