How can I implement the Pomodoro technique in my Go code to enhance cognitive concentration and prevent distractions during complex tasks that require high levels of attention, such as problem-solving, decision-making, and critical thinking?
Here is an example Go code that implements the Pomodoro technique:
package main
import (
    "fmt"
    "time"
)
func main() {
    // Set the work and break durations (in minutes)
    workDuration := 25
    breakDuration := 5
    // Set the number of cycles
    numCycles := 4
    // Start the Pomodoro cycles
    for i := 0; i < numCycles; i++ {
        // Work phase
        fmt.Printf("Work for %d minutes...\n", workDuration)
        time.Sleep(time.Duration(workDuration) * time.Minute)
        // Break phase
        fmt.Printf("Take a break for %d minutes...\n", breakDuration)
        time.Sleep(time.Duration(breakDuration) * time.Minute)
    }
    // Final message
    fmt.Println("Congratulations, you have completed all cycles!")
} 
This code uses the Pomodoro technique to break down work into focused 25-minute intervals followed by 5-minute breaks. By repeating this cycle four times, you can enhance your cognitive concentration and prevent distractions during complex tasks.

