Suppose I have 10 numbers as follows:
{8,5,1,7,13,9,11,0,10,2}
I want to sort these numbers in ascending order using an algorithm. Can you provide me with a C++ code to do so?

output:
Sure, here is a C++ code to sort the given numbers in ascending order using the bubble sort algorithm:
```
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
    int arr[] = {8,5,1,7,13,9,11,0,10,2};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    // Bubble sort algorithm
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                arr[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
    // Print the sorted array
    cout << "Sorted array in ascending order: ";
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        cout << arr[i] << " ";
    }
    return 0;
}
```
